IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-common`
IMPORT `g9-sched1-commissioner`

-- ind-c-tests-sched1: independent tests (author ind-c) of Schedule 1, the Jersey Charity Commissioner.  Row ids S1.x-nn are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md.

§ `ind-c fixtures for Schedule 1`

-- An appointment whose JAC views and notice are given as inputs; the term is fixed by its first day and the day it expires.
GIVEN appointed IS A DATE
      firstDay IS A DATE
      expires IS A DATE
      views IS A MAYBE DATE
      notice IS A MAYBE DATE
      reappointed IS A BOOLEAN
      becameMember IS A MAYBE DATE
      before IS A LIST OF `Period of service under the Schedules`
GIVETH AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
`ind-c Commissioner appointment` appointed firstDay expires views notice reappointed becameMember before MEANS
    `Appointment of the Commissioner` WITH
        `the day of the appointment` IS appointed
        `the first day of the term` IS firstDay
        `the day the term expires` IS expires
        `the person appears to the Minister to be suitable` IS TRUE
        `the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought on` IS views
        `a notice of intention was presented to the States on` IS notice
        `the person was serving as the Commissioner on the day of the appointment` IS FALSE
        `the term is followed by a re-appointment` IS reappointed
        `the day on which the person became a member of the States` IS becameMember
        `the service before this appointment` IS before

GIVEN notice IS A DATE
      appointed IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
`ind-c with notice` notice appointed MEANS
    `ind-c Commissioner appointment` appointed appointed (YMD 2032 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) (JUST notice) FALSE NOTHING EMPTY

GIVEN firstDay IS A DATE
      expires IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Appointment of the Commissioner`
`ind-c with term` firstDay expires MEANS
    `ind-c Commissioner appointment` firstDay firstDay expires (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) FALSE NOTHING EMPTY

GIVEN from IS A DATE
      stopped IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of service under the Schedules`
`ind-c service` from stopped MEANS
    `Period of service under the Schedules` WITH `first day of service` IS from, `day service stopped` IS stopped, `as a designated relevant person` IS FALSE

GIVEN given IS A DATE
      effective IS A DATE
      inWriting IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice of resignation of the Commissioner`
`ind-c resignation` given effective inWriting MEANS
    `Notice of resignation of the Commissioner` WITH
        `the day the notice was given` IS given
        `the notice is in writing and given to the Minister` IS inWriting
        `the day the resignation takes effect` IS effective

GIVEN first IS A MAYBE DATE
      last IS A MAYBE DATE
      absent IS A BOOLEAN
      bankrupt IS A BOOLEAN
      ill IS A BOOLEAN
      unfit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner`
`ind-c grounds` first last absent bankrupt ill unfit MEANS
    `Grounds for terminating the appointment of the Commissioner` WITH
        `the first day of absence from duties` IS first
        `the last day of absence from duties` IS last
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person has been absent for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` IS absent
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person has become bankrupt` IS bankrupt
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person is incapacitated by illness` IS ill
        `the Minister is satisfied that the person is otherwise unable or unfit to discharge the functions of the Commissioner` IS unfit

GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      provided IS A MAYBE DATE
      prepared IS A BOOLEAN
      published IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Report of the Commissioner on a calendar year`
`ind-c report` year provided prepared published MEANS
    `Report of the Commissioner on a calendar year` WITH
        `the calendar year` IS year
        `the Commissioner has prepared the report` IS prepared
        `the Commissioner has published the report` IS published
        `the day on which the report was provided to the Minister` IS provided
        `the report was provided as soon as practicable after the end of the year` IS TRUE
        `the day on which the Minister laid a copy before the States` IS NOTHING
        `the copy was laid as soon as practicable after the Minister received the report` IS TRUE

GIVEN subject IS A `Subject of a decision of the Commissioner`
      outcome IS AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`ind-c decision` subject outcome MEANS `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS subject, outcome IS outcome

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Schedules 1 and 2`
      subject IS A `Subject of a decision of the Commissioner`
      outcome IS AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
      authorised IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-c staff may` interp subject outcome authorised MEANS
    `Sch 1 para 4(3) a member of the Commissioner's staff may exercise the function on behalf of the Commissioner` interp (`ind-c decision` subject outcome) authorised

GIVETH AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
`ind-c does` MEANS `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
GIVETH AN `Outcome of a decision of the Commissioner`
`ind-c refuses` MEANS `the Commissioner refuses`

§ `ind-c Schedule 1 paragraph 1 -- appointment`

-- S1.1-02: the JAC's views before appointing
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(2) the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before the appointment` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c Commissioner appointment` (YMD 2026 1 20) (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2032 2 1) NOTHING (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) FALSE NOTHING EMPTY)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(2) the views of the Jersey Appointments Commission were sought before the appointment` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c Commissioner appointment` (YMD 2026 1 20) (YMD 2026 2 1) (YMD 2032 2 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 5)) (JUST (YMD 2026 1 1)) FALSE NOTHING EMPTY)
-- S1.1-03 (pre-committed ambiguous; reading A taken): notice 1 January, appointment 15 January
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with notice` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 15))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.1 is read as B` (`ind-c with notice` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 15))
-- S1.1-04 .. S1.1-08
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with notice` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 14))
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with notice` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 16))
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.1 is read as B` (`ind-c with notice` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 16))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with notice` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with notice` (YMD 2026 1 20) (YMD 2026 1 15))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c Commissioner appointment` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2032 1 1) (JUST (YMD 2025 12 1)) NOTHING FALSE NOTHING EMPTY)
-- S1.1-09: across a leap February
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with notice` (YMD 2028 2 20) (YMD 2028 3 5))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(3) the notice of intention was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with notice` (YMD 2028 2 20) (YMD 2028 3 4))
-- S1.1-10 .. S1.1-12: not more than 6 years (the end date is the day the term expires, F9.2 A)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with term` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with term` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 2))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with term` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 4 1))
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with term` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2027 3 1))
-- S1.1-13 (pre-committed ambiguous): a term from 29 February 2024; ind-c's reading A (clamp)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with term` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2030 2 28))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c with term` (YMD 2024 2 29) (YMD 2030 3 1))
-- F9.2 B (the end date is the last day of the term), by that reading's definition
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.2 is read as B` (`ind-c with term` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 2 29))
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(5) the period of the appointment is within the limit` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.2 is read as B` (`ind-c with term` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2032 3 1))
-- S1.1-16: the duty to keep the office filled
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 1(7) the Minister has complied with the duty to keep the office filled` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(7) the Minister has complied with the duty to keep the office filled` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 1(7) the Minister has complied with the duty to keep the office filled` TRUE FALSE

§ `ind-c Schedule 1 paragraph 2 -- status and the Dormant Bank Accounts words`

-- S1.2-04: remuneration out of the annual income of the States; from 16 December 2019 subject to Article 20(1) DBA Law
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 31 May 2019`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 16 December 2019`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `the text of 2 October 2026`
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 2(4)(a) the remuneration of the Commissioner must be paid out of the annual income of the States` `the favoured interpretation` `the text of 1 January 2019` TRUE
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 2(4)(a) the remuneration of the Commissioner must be paid out of the annual income of the States` `the favoured interpretation` `the text of 2 October 2026` FALSE
-- S1.2-04b (pre-committed ambiguous): before any consolidated text; reading B refuses (ind-c's reading A is in ind-c-tests-ambiguous.l4)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Sch 1 and 2: the Dormant Bank Accounts words are in the text of` `before the first consolidated version`
-- S1.4-12: the same words in 4(7)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 4(7) the cost of providing staff, accommodation and equipment must be met out of the annual income of the States` `the favoured interpretation` `the text of 31 May 2019` TRUE

§ `ind-c Schedule 1 paragraph 3 -- termination`

-- S1.3-01 (pre-committed ambiguous on 15 April; reading A taken)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 4 15) TRUE) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 4 15)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 4 14) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 4 16) TRUE) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 4 16)
-- S1.3-02 (pre-committed ambiguous on 28 February): clamp (A) against rollover (F9.3 C)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2025 11 30) (YMD 2026 2 28) TRUE) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.3 is read as C` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2025 11 30) (YMD 2026 2 28) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.3 is read as C` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2025 11 30) (YMD 2026 3 2) TRUE) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 3 2)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2025 11 30) (YMD 2026 2 27) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S1.3-03: a leap year
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2027 11 30) (YMD 2028 2 29) TRUE) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2028 2 29)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2027 11 30) (YMD 2028 2 28) TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- S1.3-04: not in writing to the Minister
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- F9.3 B (the office ends when the notice is given), by that reading's definition
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(1)(a) the day the office ends by resignation` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.3 is read as B` (`ind-c resignation` (YMD 2026 1 15) (YMD 2026 4 15) TRUE) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- S1.3-05: absence longer than 4 consecutive weeks (28 days is not; 29 is)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 28)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 29)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 3(2)(a) the person has been absent from duties for a period longer than 4 consecutive weeks` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.4 is read as B` (`ind-c grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 29)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S1.3-06, S1.3-07: the grounds and the Minister's satisfaction
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 29)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 29)) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c grounds` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c grounds` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c grounds` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation` (`ind-c grounds` NOTHING NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(2) the Minister has satisfied himself or herself on a ground for terminating` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.19 is read as B` (`ind-c grounds` (JUST (YMD 2026 3 1)) (JUST (YMD 2026 3 20)) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- S1.3-08 (pre-committed ambiguous on 15 March; reading A taken)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(3) the notice of the termination was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(3) the notice of the termination was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 14)
#ASSERT `Sch 1 para 3(3) the notice of the termination was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT `Sch 1 para 3(3) the notice of the termination was presented to the States in time` `the favoured interpretation, but F9.5 is read as B` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 15)
